  "student_passage": "My (1) ____ is making a small greenhouse for his plants. He has a plan on a large piece of paper. He (2) ____ each wooden piece twice before he cuts it. I am not allowed to use the sharp tools, but I can hold the paper and read the numbers to him.\n\nThe roof will be made of (3) ____, so we put on thick (4) ____ before moving the panels. Grandfather tells me to be (5) ____ near the edges. We put the panels on a blanket while he checks the wooden frame.\n\nThere is a narrow path (6) ____ the garden. We carry the frame along it and place it beside the wall. The plants will get plenty of light there. The room already looks (7) ____ when the afternoon sun reaches the wall.\n\nWe (8) ____ stop for a drink when the weather is warm, but we never leave the loose panels standing on the path. We check that everything is safe (9) ____ we go inside. It takes longer to build something when I help, Grandfather says, but he likes having company. I am happy when we can (10) ____ on a project instead of sitting in different rooms.",
