  "filled_passage": "My (1) grandfather is making a small greenhouse for his plants. He has a plan on a large piece of paper. He (2) measures each wooden piece twice before he cuts it. I am not allowed to use the sharp tools, but I can hold the paper and read the numbers to him.\n\nThe roof will be made of (3) glass, so we put on thick (4) gloves before moving the panels. Grandfather tells me to be (5) careful near the edges. We put the panels on a blanket while he checks the wooden frame.\n\nThere is a narrow path (6) across the garden. We carry the frame along it and place it beside the wall. The plants will get plenty of light there. The room already looks (7) bright when the afternoon sun reaches the wall.\n\nWe (8) sometimes stop for a drink when the weather is warm, but we never leave the loose panels standing on the path. We check that everything is safe (9) before we go inside. It takes longer to build something when I help, Grandfather says, but he likes having company. I am happy when we can (10) work together on a project instead of sitting in different rooms.",
